      "text": "We begin by drawing a right triangle and labeling sides $AD = 3$, $CD = \\sqrt{13} - 3$, and $BC = 2$.\nTo calculate $\\tan V$, we need to calculate ratio $AD : BC$, or $\\frac{3}{2}$, so $\\tan V = \\boxed{\\frac{3}{2}}$.\n\n[asy]\npair V,W,X;\nW = (0,0);\nV = (0,3);\nX = (2,0);\ndraw(V--W--X--V);\ndraw(rightanglemark(V,W,X,7));\nlabel(\"$V$\",V,N);\nlabel(\"$W$\",W,NW);\nlabel(\"$X$\",X,SE);\nlabel(\"$3$\",midpoint(V--W),NW);\nlabel(\"$\\sqrt{13}$\",midpoint(V--X),NE);\nlabel(\"$AD$\",midpoint(V--W),NW, blue);\nlabel(\"$BC$\",midpoint(V--X),SE, red);\nlabel(\"$\\frac{3}{2}$\", blue, red, red, red, right, red, blue, blue, red, blue, red, blue);\n[/asy] To solve for \\(\\tan V\\) in the given right triangle \\(VWX\\), we need to first determine the length of the hypotenuse \\(WX\\) using the Pythagorean theorem. Given that \\(VX = \\sqrt{13}\\) and \\(VW = 3\\), we have the equation:\n\n\\[\nVX^2 + VW^2 = WX^2\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the given values:\n\n\\[\n(\\sqrt{13})^2 + 3^2 = WX^2\n\\]\n\nCalculating the squares:\n\n\\[\n13 + 9 = WX^2\n\\]\n\n\\[\n22 = WX^2\n\\]\n\nTaking the square root of both sides:\n\n\\[\nWX = \\sqrt{22}\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to find \\(\\tan V\\). By definition, \\(\\tan V\\) is the ratio of the opposite side to the adjacent side in the right triangle. Here, the opposite side \\(VW\\) (along the x-axis) and the adjacent side \\(XW - VW\\) (opposite angle \\(V\\)).\n\nCalculate \\(XW\\):\n\n\\[\nXW = VX = \\sqrt{13}\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\nXW - VW = \\sqrt{13} - 3\n\\]\n\nNow, we can find \\(\\tan V\\):\n\n\\[\n\\tan V = \\frac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{adjacent}} = \\frac{VW}{XW - VW}\n\\]\n\nSubstitute the known values:\n\n\\[\n\\tan V = \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13} - 3}\n\\]\n\nHowever, it is often more convenient to rationalize the denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\tan V = \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13} - 3} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{13} + 3}{\\sqrt{13} + 3}\n\\]\n\nSimplify the expression:\n\n\\[\n\\tan V = \\frac{3(\\sqrt{13} + 3)}{13 - 9}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\tan V = \\frac{3(\\sqrt{13} + 3)}{4}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{3}{2}}\n\\]",
